# Docker build context excludes — Docker does NOT read .gitignore, so secrets and
# bulky/build artifacts must be listed here explicitly or they get COPYied into
# the image (the Dockerfile does `COPY apps/server ./apps/server`).

# Secrets / local env — never bake into an image
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Dependencies & build output (reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/out

# VCS, logs, editor, local tooling
.git
**/*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode-test

# Terraform local artifacts — the build context is the repo root, so the 200MB+
# provider cache and any local/backend state would otherwise be sent to the Docker
# daemon (and state must never enter a build context). Not COPYied, just excluded.
**/.terraform
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/errored.tfstate
